# Observability Rules

Use structured Pino logs.

Every request should have a correlation/trace ID.

Log useful fields:

- requestId
- traceId
- operation
- actorId when appropriate
- tenantId/vendorId/storeId when safe
- durationMs
- outcome
- errorCode

Never log credentials or tokens.

## Tracing

Use OpenTelemetry around:

- HTTP requests
- database operations
- Redis operations
- BullMQ jobs
- payment provider calls
- search calls
- object storage calls

## Errors

Use Sentry for actionable exceptions.

Do not capture sensitive request bodies blindly.

## Metrics

Measure business and technical health:

- checkout success/failure
- payment callback success/failure
- order creation latency
- queue lag
- inventory reservation conflicts
- DB latency
- Redis latency
- search indexing lag
- payout failures

Dashboards and alerts should reflect SLOs, not just infrastructure CPU.
